error[X0526]: calling `plain` isn't allowed in a `constexpr` function
  --> constexpr-objects.xn:13:56
   |
13 |   public constexpr function usesPlain():Float const => plain()            // `plain` isn't constexpr
   |          ---------                                     ^^^^^^^ not `constexpr`
   |          |
   |          `constexpr` here
   |
   = note: allowed: parameters and locals, `this` and its fields, literals, operators, `?:`, conversions like `int()`, inline constants, `Math` functions, `String` methods like `trim` and `replace`, `constexpr` functions, methods and constructors, and the statements `if`, `while`, `for`, `switch`, `return`, `break` and `continue`

error[X0523]: an inline constant can't hold an object
  --> constexpr-objects.xn:18:45
   |
18 |   public static inline final ORIGIN:Point = new Point(0, 0)             // an inline constant can't hold an object
   |                              ------         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an object built at compile time
   |                              |
   |                              `ORIGIN` is declared `inline`
   |
   = note: an inline constant is pasted into the code: it must be a number, `String` or `Boolean`; use `static final` for an object

error[X0723]: `Base.size` is `constexpr` and can't be overridden
  --> constexpr-objects.xn:29:28
   |
25 |   public constexpr function size():int => 1
   |          --------- declared `constexpr` here
...
29 |   override public function size():int { return 2 }                        // a constexpr method is implicitly final
   |                            ^^^^
   |
   = note: a `constexpr` method is implicitly `final`: calls of it may be computed at compile time, so no subclass can replace it
